SUMMARY:Cooking and Baking Class – September 2026
DESCRIPTION:Cook. Learn. Belong.\nStep into the kitchen and discover the joy of cooking together. This free\, hands-on monthly class invites youth ages 5–22 who are blind or low vision—and their families—to build essential kitchen skills in a welcoming\, confidence-building space. \nLed by our O&M/ADL Specialist\, Ruby Cabral\, each session blends practical instruction with real-world techniques\, empowering participants to move safely\, independently\, and creatively in the kitchen. Together\, families will prepare simple\, delicious recipes while strengthening skills that extend far beyond the stove. \nClasses take place in the Lighthouse kitchen\, located next to The Lighthouse at 820 Marston Street. \nAll tools and ingredients are provided. No experience required—just curiosity\, connection\, and an appetite to learn. \nThis September\, we’ll be cooking: Pumpkin Snickerdoodle Cookies! \nRegistration is required. Come ready to stir\, explore\, and grow—one meal at a time. \nSign Up Is Now Closed
URL:https://houstonlighthouse.org/event/cooking-and-baking-class-september-2026/
LOCATION:The Lighthouse of Houston\, 3602 West Dallas\, Houston\, TX\, 77019\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Events,Youth Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://eadn-wc02-10923896.nxedge.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/BakingCooking-Class.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Ruby Cabral%2C O&M/ADL Specialist%2C The Lighthouse of Houston":MAILTO:ecabral@houstonlighthouse.org
